 "title": "ISAA- Official Site",
 "text": "ISAA- Official Site\nSkip to main content\nAbout the Office\nAssessors of Iowa (Map)\nCommittees & Boards\nConstitution & By-Laws\nDistricts\nHistory of Assessors\nInstitute of Iowa Certified Assessors (IICA)\nMedia & Publications\nOur Strategic Plan\nForms\nCredits and Exemptions\nISAA Presidents\nOutstanding Members\nAppointment and Budget\nAppointment Requirements\nDuties of the Assessor\nImportant Dates for the Office\nMarket Value\nMisconceptions About the Office\nNotification and Appeal\nWhy Do Values Change?\nCentral District\nEast Central District\nNorth Central District\nNortheast District\nNorthwest District\nSouth Central District\nSoutheast District\nSouthwest District\nCommittees - Standing\nCommittees - Ad Hoc\nOther Committees\nIowa Dept of Revenue Appointed Committees\nAudit\nEducation\nExecutive Board\nExemptions\nHistorian\nIPERS\nLegislative\nManual & Forms\nNominating\nPR/Editorial\nProgram\nWays & Means\nWeb/IT\nHands-on-Training/Mentoring\nRenewable Energy\nIDR Assessor Education\nIDR E-Abstract & Recon\nIDR E-DOV\nIDR Preliminary Educational Requirement\nIAAO Representatives\nISAC Director\nISAC Legislative Policy\nNACo\nNCRAAO\nStrategic Planning\nVCS User Group\nCreation of the IICA\nBoard of Directors\nConstitution, By-Laws, Rules & Code of Ethics\nMembership\nPast Directors / Officers\nAnnual Conference Page\nICA Course Descriptions\nICA Designation Presentation\nPast Directors\nPast Presidents\nPast Secretary-Treasurer\nPast Vice-Presidents\nPublications\nIn the news...\nVideos\nMore from individual offices!\nAssessment Appeal Forms\nCredit & Exemption Forms\nMobile/Manufactured Home Forms\n2014 Conference\n2015 Conference\n2016 Conference\n2017 Conference\n2018 Conference\nAg Land Use Adjustment\nDistrict Court\nmenu\nISAA\nHome\nAbout the ISAA\nResources\nForms and Manuals\nLinks\nPrevious Next\nmenu\nAbout the ISAA\nResources\nForms and Manuals\nLinks\nAssessors of Iowa\nCredits & Exemptions\nHistory of Assessors\nCareer Opportunities\nFAQs\nMedia & Publications\nWhere Do Your Property Tax Dollars Go? (video)\nCalendar of Events\nLog in\nWelcome to the Iowa State Association of Assessors\nLindsey Thomas\nISAA President\nthomas@mahaskacountyia.gov\nThe mission of the Iowa State Association of Assessors is to\npromote excellence in property valuation by ensuring fair and equitable\nassessments for property owners and local governments throughout the State of\nIowa. Our core values—Integrity, Professionalism,\nFairness, and Trustworthiness—guide our work and\ndecision-making.\nMembers of the Iowa\nState Association of Assessors collaborate to achieve and maintain the highest\nstandards in property assessment administration through ongoing\nprofessionalism, education, and effective communication. We are committed to\npromoting the public good by ensuring equitable assessments and enhancing\npublic understanding of Iowa’s property assessment process. In partnership with\nthe Iowa Department of Revenue, Iowa\nassessors pursue continuing education and work collectively to improve the\nquality, consistency, and uniformity of assessments statewide.\nThis website was\ndeveloped as an educational resource to foster a better understanding of the\nappraisal and assessment process. It includes information on the duties of the\nassessor, office responsibilities, available credits and exemptions, frequently\nasked questions, useful links, and contact information for each of Iowa’s seven\ncity assessors and 99 county assessors. Additionally, the site provides\nassessment professionals with tools to share information, stay informed about\nchanges in construction methods and real estate markets, and further develop\nstandards and procedures in support of the Association’s vision.\nOur Vision is to create\nthe highest standard of professionalism in our membership through\ncollaboration, mentoring, and education. To attain fairness, equity, and\nuniformity in property assessments throughout the State of Iowa.\nWe encourage property\nowners to contact their local assessor with any questions, suggestions, or\nconcerns.\nContact Us |\nAccessibility |\nSite Map\nGovernment Websites by Municipal One ®",
